{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term","id":66728,"title":"Why are the Lunars \"Celestial Exalted\" as we understand the term?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-06T14:26:11-08:00","id":66728,"title":"Why are the Lunars \"Celestial Exalted\" as we understand the term?","content":"Aside from the fact that Luna pretty much has to be the patron of shapeshifting, half-beast heroes, and Luna is a Celestial Incarnae like the Sun and Stars, what are the compelling reasons for the Lunar Exalted Host to renew itself through reincarnation instead of reproduction?<br /> <br /> Why are they more like Solars than like Dragon-Blooded?<br /> <br /> What stories and archetypes does this facilitate? In modern literature, at least, the idea of shapeshifting beastfolk is that it is a hereditary state, leading to the formation of clans or entire societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:38:23-08:00","id":66742,"title":"","content":"I dunno, werewolves passing on lycanthropy via bite is more akin to Exaltation than heredity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:51:26-08:00","id":66752,"title":"","content":"I... don't think there is a particular other reason? I mean, you've hit the nail on the head there, in that the Lunars are Celestials because of their patron Luna. That's really about it. <br /> <br /> Or, since that's probably not enough, I can think of two reasons. The first is that power passed down through the blood is pretty strongly tied to the Dragon-Blooded. It's one of their defining traits as a species. Borrowing that ideal for the Lunars as well means that the concept is no longer unique, and the two variants of Exalted end up pretty much being defined by 'these ones uses elements, and these ones use animals for their thematic statements', which I think would be a mistake. <br /> <br /> Secondly, Lunars are not just shapeshifters in the same sense as, say, that village of secret werewolves. They are (conceptually, at least) the ULTIMATE shape-shifters, capable of adopting just about any form they might want, including that of gods, demons and strange not-things from beyond the edges of reality. More than that, they can freely modify those 'templates', adjusting values like size or mixing them together to create unique monsters that stalk the edges of the civilized world. You can't really have that and call yourself a species, because the one and only commonality then would be that they all use a particular flavour of essence. And that's a defining characteristic to groups more on the order of taxonomical classifications, like 'gods', 'ghosts' and 'carbon-based lifeforms'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1354-grey-seer","name":"Grey Seer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:55:36-08:00","id":66757,"title":"","content":"I was going to type up something long, but the forum software has pissed me off, so I pose this question to you. Why aren't the Solars a vast quantity of utterly clueless saps and patsies beyond any limit? And why aren't all of the Dawns homicidally insane, intent on killing the Dragon-Blooded and other Exalted by any means which they deem necessary and ignoring all collateral damage, like the Wayward Creed? And why aren't the members of the Zenith and/or Eclipse Castes barely functional vessels of the beings responsible for the rash of new Solar Exaltations, like the Hermits?<br /> <br /> Modern literature is skewed a certain way. To that end, it's probably going to get ignored in favor of mythological parallels, like Fafnir stealing a bunch of gold and turning into a dragon to protect it, any given hero in anime letting loose some formerly restrained portion of themselves which is monstrous and likened to a raging beast, or Enkidu wrestling Gilgamesh to a bara-tinged draw as the champion of the wilderness against civilization (prior to having a bunch of sex and getting drunk, anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:56:10-08:00","id":66758,"title":"","content":"Because power that can be passed through the blood is less powerful. Lunars are supposed to be more powerful than Terrestrials, so there should be fewer of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:57:00-08:00","id":66759,"title":"","content":"If I had to guess, it would be for a couple reasons:<br /> <br /> 1.) there is a definite vein to be mined in the Sun-moon dichotomy, and IMHO it's more meaningful for a reincarated young hero to meet her reincarnated friend/love/self-appointed guardian, rather than to meet someone who merely bears the bloodline of the same. That's really a story that's mined pretty well with the Dragon-Blooded, and I do not believe the Lunar narrative gains anything frm it.<br /> <br /> 2.) The things Lunars are is ultimately singular. They might beget hordes, but they are not a horde in and of themselves. If they are referred to as a collective, it is only in the same sense that the legenday God-Kings of the First Age are: they fit a rough category, but each is their own thing.*<br /> <br /> 3.) The idea that their power comes from a Bloodline also suggests something that the current ruling structure of Creation doesn't immediately suggest: that they can be exterminated. And as much as the Lunar Exalted have that strong Survivor angle, the idea that their bloodline can be purged is kind of horrifying and I don't think it belongs here.<br /> <br /> <br /> * This really applies to some degree to all Exalted, even the Dragonblooded. In the Terrestrials' case, though, the idea that they spring from the blood and from family are deeply ingrained into the splat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:59:13-08:00","id":66762,"title":"","content":"I would say, because the Moon is the counterpart and companion to the Sun. (And I'm not talking about Bonds here, or about Luna and UCS spesifically, but about broader symbolic associations.) You can't have that if they're not the same order of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:00:12-08:00","id":66764,"title":"","content":"When they're presenting the Sun-Moon duality thing as a special relationship, the reincarnation helps facilitate recurrence of attachment in that considering that the Solars are supposed to have been gone for a long time.<br /> <br /> Also, if they're making the Lunars more bitter about their fall from the First Age, them having memories and sensations from what they've lost is useful for giving credibility to that.<br /> <br /> And if they're going to be as powerful, it seems preferable to keep their numbers small, without their being a means to reduce them.<br /> <br /> How would reproduction as a means of renewing them work? Like, could your children Exalt while you were still alive as entirely new things, or would it need to wait until you had died and then a descendent could come into it? The former implies expansion more than renewal.<br /> <br /> Although I do like how the Okami have the thing where they reincarnate, but if they find their soul mate and sleep with them, the child will be a brand new Okami.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:08:57-08:00","id":66773,"title":"","content":"If there <i>were</i> races of simple two-species &quot;natural&quot; shapeshifters in Creation, hereditary werewolves or wereboars or whatever, you could point at them and say, &quot;Lunars are Celestials because they are as far from those guys as Solars are from ordinary mortal humans&quot;. Without them, and with the closest analog being animal-men who can't change shape at all, it's a little harder to see, but fundamentally it's still true. Turning into a wolf-man when the moon comes out is about as significant to a Lunar as forging a steak knife would be to a Solar weaponsmith.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that real-world mythological <i>Solar</i> archetypes don't tend to &quot;Exalt&quot; either. Achilles, Perseus, and so on could be said to inherit their power from their heroic or godly lineages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:18:13-08:00","id":66781,"title":"","content":"Lunars are the most fleshy focused of the Celestials. Sometimes, sex and breeding feel as important to them as it does the Dragon-Blooded. They rarely feel as big and important as the Solar variants, the Siderials, or the Alchemicals (in Authcthnon).<br /> <br /> Yes, they're Celestial Exalts, but they feel like a liminal case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:28:25-08:00","id":66791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66781#post66781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are the most fleshy focused of the Celestials. Sometimes, sex and breeding feel as important to them as it does the Dragon-Blooded. They rarely feel as big and important as the Solar variants, the Siderials, or the Alchemicals (in Authcthnon).<br /> <br /> Yes, they're Celestial Exalts, but they feel like a liminal case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely Liminals are the liminal case...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:35:46-08:00","id":66795,"title":"","content":"They receive their Exaltation from on high, by the decree of Luna when she deems a mortal worthy of her blessing. As such, they're Celestial Exalted. Seems straightforward enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:45:16-08:00","id":66803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term#post66728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What stories and archetypes does this facilitate? In modern literature, at least, the idea of shapeshifting beastfolk is that it is a hereditary state, leading to the formation of clans or entire societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern literature is generally a poor place to seek epic inspiration. In classical literature the archetype of the monster is near-solitary. The existence of these creatures at the fringes of a society define many of its taboos and shape the direction of those societies without the societies even realizing it. Often even the chroniclers miss it. Think about how the existence of all those sea monsters determined the way the Greeks navigated the Aegean. Homer never even really bothered to mention it beyond pointing out that the reason these Greeks had so much trouble is that they hadn't heeded the common wisdom about which ways to sail. The reader is assumed to know about these proscriptions.<br /> <br /> Lunars are less &quot;friendly neighborhood werewolf&quot; and more &quot;monster that lurks in the shadowed corners of the world and keeps everyone on the lit side of the street.&quot; They're the embodiment of ethos. They're also the leash to a Solar's pathos, but this has been poorly or entirely mis-represented for a while now. It's not strictly something that needs to be in the game, but when executed properly can provide a lot of fertile ground for storytelling.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are the embodiment of logos, for the record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T18:17:28-08:00","id":66870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66758#post66758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because power that can be passed through the blood is less powerful. Lunars are supposed to be more powerful than Terrestrials, so there should be fewer of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize; I took it as assumed that Lunars who propagate through breeding would and should be less powerful than Lunars who reincarnate.<br /> \u200b<br /> Given the strong similarities between Solar and Lunar source material, I am just as unsure why the Lunar Exalted should be as strong as they are as I am unsure about their reincarnation.<br /> <br /> A form of Lunar Exalted who operate more like Terrestrials than Solars would be much more distinct from Terrestrials than the Celestial Lunar Exalted are distinct from the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I'm curious about how the Lunar Exalted will be distinguished from the Solar Exalted they resemble so much. Or perhaps I'm just getting confused by the similarity of source materials again, and missing the forest for the trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-06-2014, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T18:56:36-08:00","id":66884,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure there's much to this beyond &quot;Because that's how they were initially conceived and executed.&quot; They're the long-lost complimenting partners and spouses of the Solar Exalted; people complain about the Lunar bond, but long before the Lunar bond was a thing, the 1e castebooks were all &quot;Solars and Lunars often engaged in diplomatic marriages, some of which blossomed into True Love -- as a returning Solar, you might have an ancient Lunar out there who remembers your previous incarnation and might be drawn to you in some fashion!&quot; Considering that was a direction they wanted to run with, what would have been the point of making Lunars a more numerous, less powerful sort of Exalt?<br /> <br /> And now, of course, what would be the point of changing it? And just how angry would Lunar fans get if we did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T18:57:13-08:00","id":66885,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure there's much to this beyond &quot;Because that's how they were initially conceived and executed.&quot; They're the long-lost complimenting partners and spouses of the Solar Exalted; people complain about the Lunar bond, but long before the Lunar bond was a thing, the 1e castebooks were all &quot;Solars and Lunars often engaged in diplomatic marriages, some of which blossomed into True Love -- as a returning Solar, you might have an ancient Lunar out there who remembers your previous incarnation and might be drawn to you in some fashion!&quot; Considering that was a direction they wanted to run with, what would have been the point of making Lunars a more numerous, less powerful sort of Exalt?<br /> And now, of course, what would be the point of changing it? And just how angry would Lunar fans get if we did?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:14:00-08:00","id":66899,"title":"","content":"I dunno guys, the answer seems pretty intuitive - if you're gonna make a story up about sky gods, then the moon is gonna rank pretty high up there.<br /> <br /> Have you seen the sky? That thing is all up in there! Big and round and shiny! And hey, isn't it weird it's almost exactly the same size as the sun? And they get together sometimes?!?<br /> <br /> That may be like 8 year old logic but it's still applicable in this case I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:17:28-08:00","id":66904,"title":"","content":"I can't think of a way to make the Lunars interesting if &quot;lunarism&quot; is an inherited condition.<br /> <br /> I mean it, I got nuthin'. If they're a generic &quot;race&quot; of crossbreeding shapeshifters, then their only obvious purpose in the setting will be to be or generate monsters for other Exalts to fight. They might as well not be protagonists at all, because the elements that make them special - namely, exaltation-as-a-reward-for-heroism, reincarnation (and associated baggage), association with Luna (how strongly are the DBs connected to the actual Dragons, really?), and the famous/infamous Lunar Bond - would all be gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:30:40-08:00","id":66913,"title":"","content":"I think Lunars have more in common with Arachne and Medusa than modern werewolves; mortals who were transformed into monsters by the power of the gods. Only, you know, without the petty Greek spite. <br /> <br /> Hereditary power would have different connotations. What is missing from the Terrestrial bloodlines that could be added to the setting with a new type of Exalt, and what hole would the current Lunars leave if they were removed or significantly changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T00:26:52-08:00","id":67025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66884#post66884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure there's much to this beyond &quot;Because that's how they were initially conceived and executed.&quot; They're the long-lost complimenting partners and spouses of the Solar Exalted; people complain about the Lunar bond, but long before the Lunar bond was a thing, the 1e castebooks were all &quot;Solars and Lunars often engaged in diplomatic marriages, some of which blossomed into True Love -- as a returning Solar, you might have an ancient Lunar out there who remembers your previous incarnation and might be drawn to you in some fashion!&quot; Considering that was a direction they wanted to run with, what would have been the point of making Lunars a more numerous, less powerful sort of Exalt?<br /> <br /> And now, of course, what would be the point of changing it? And just how angry would Lunar fans get if we did?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also note tht lunars originally werne't intended to be a playable character, so there's that. As for how angry... you <i>did</i> see the incredible hulk right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T00:30:03-08:00","id":67026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66904#post66904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of a way to make the Lunars interesting if &quot;lunarism&quot; is an inherited condition.<br /> <br /> I mean it, I got nuthin'. If they're a generic &quot;race&quot; of crossbreeding shapeshifters, then their only obvious purpose in the setting will be to be or generate monsters for other Exalts to fight. They might as well not be protagonists at all, because the elements that make them special - namely, exaltation-as-a-reward-for-heroism, reincarnation (and associated baggage), association with Luna (how strongly are the DBs connected to the actual Dragons, really?), and the famous/infamous Lunar Bond - would all be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there could be a VAST number of ways you could make them interesting-- for instance, the idea of the &quot;silver pact&quot; becomes a lot more important if you're dragonblooded power level and the idea that lunars can't just walk in and take over places and so have to work within existing societies also becomes more effective-- if you can't monster out into godzilla, having to actually listent to a barbarian warlord makes a lot more sense. <br /> <br /> So yeah, it's a way that you can make them extremely interesting...BUT.<br /> <br /> It's not at all compatible with where they are now. At best, it'd be a shard idea, but as the lunars are set up now, they have to be celestial level. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T01:43:16-08:00","id":67050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66899#post66899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the sky? That thing is all up in there! Big and round and shiny!</div> </div> </div> </div>And not just shiny, but <i>solid</i>; it has surface features visible to the naked eye!<br /> <br /> John once said that the moon was unlike anything else in the sky, and it took me a while to get that the moon looks like an actual <i>object</i>, suspended up there, rather than a varying sized ball of light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T04:00:13-08:00","id":67097,"title":"","content":"Like the sun, the moon rises and sets in an endless eternal cycle.<br /> <br /> Also, the game needs a surviving outsider Celestial type who was present for the past 700 years for the Wyld Hunt to really make sense. Terrestrial Lunars would massively change the nature of the Wyld Hunt in ways that probably wouldn't jive well with how it's supposed to interact with returning Solars (since it would no longer really make sense for it to be designed to fight Celestials.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:03:52-08:00","id":67167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=67050#post67050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And not just shiny, but <i>solid</i>; it has surface features visible to the naked eye!<br /> <br /> John once said that the moon was unlike anything else in the sky, and it took me a while to get that the moon looks like an actual <i>object</i>, suspended up there, rather than a varying sized ball of light.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does make the moon uniquely suited for association with a splat whose aesthetics are supposed to include &quot;carved bone and rough stone&quot;. The moon itself is an enormous, shiny but rough <i>rock</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:35:50-08:00","id":67184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66913#post66913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is missing from the Terrestrial bloodlines that could be added to the setting with a new type of Exalt, and what hole would the current Lunars leave if they were removed or significantly changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Picking this up again now that I've thought about it some more.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded emphasize familial bond, so you'd want to do something different, probably playing off the concept of blood brothers. Sworn brotherhoods kind of cover that niche, but I think they're closer to an affirmation of the family bond that connects all Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Anyway, blood brothers. You now have a form of Exaltation that can be spread from one friend to another through their blood and their mutual loyalty. That covers the modern werewolf infection. It also means that, unlike the Dragon-Blooded, they don't have any obligation towards their all of their Exalted kin, just towards their closest blood brothers. That's something new that the Dragon-Blooded don't cover.<br /> <br /> That leaves the question of what to do with Lunars. Conan the Barbarian, Kull the Conqueror, Khal Drogo, Genghis Khan, Khan Noonien Singh... Lunars aren't just barbarians, they're barbarian kings, the mightiest champions who are able to unite warring tribes into a single horde. They're meant to be far mightier than the common rabble, to be Exalted above all others. That's what gives them a mystique of command and rulership. They can't do that if their Exaltation is passed through bonds of friendship. This also fits into their relationship with Solars; the Sun and Moon both stand far above the earth.<br /> <br /> So there's room for a kind of &quot;hereditary&quot; shapeshifter, but it can't really be based on Lunars. I'd recommend something to do with animal gods or Gaia, but that would be redundant with Exigents or Dragon-Blooded. <br /> <br /> How about giving Creation itself its own Exalted champions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:42:12-08:00","id":67189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=66904#post66904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of a way to make the Lunars interesting if &quot;lunarism&quot; is an inherited condition.<br /> <br /> I mean it, I got nuthin'. If they're a generic &quot;race&quot; of crossbreeding shapeshifters, then their only obvious purpose in the setting will be to be or generate monsters for other Exalts to fight. They might as well not be protagonists at all, because the elements that make them special - namely, exaltation-as-a-reward-for-heroism, reincarnation (and associated baggage), association with Luna (how strongly are the DBs connected to the actual Dragons, really?), and the famous/infamous Lunar Bond - would all be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am, for the record, not in favor of making Lunars non-Celestial Exalted. That said, this post baffles me.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you take a splat, change a trait that causes some other characteristics that depended on it to either fall off or change enormously, <i>and then don't hang new characteristics onto the changed trait</i>, then yes, you do indeed probably get something much less interesting. Would anyone seriously expect otherwise?<br /> <br /> That said, putting aside how the first two &quot;elements that make them special&quot; apply to Solars -- and therefore don't make Lunars special -- the other two wouldn't necessarily need to be dropped. For instance, translated to Lunar-Exaltation-as-inheritance, the idea that every single one among not just 300 but scores of Lunar Exalts has had a personal encounter with Luna is something I can actually buy, given her nature, and could create a very interesting and distinctive cultural effect (in a way that feels different from when there are only 300 of them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T13:44:41-08:00","id":67393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=67184#post67184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leaves the question of what to do with Lunars. Conan the Barbarian, Kull the Conqueror, Khal Drogo, Genghis Khan, Khan Noonien Singh... Lunars aren't just barbarians, they're barbarian kings, the mightiest champions who are able to unite warring tribes into a single horde. They're meant to be far mightier than the common rabble, to be Exalted above all others. That's what gives them a mystique of command and rulership. They can't do that if their Exaltation is passed through bonds of friendship. This also fits into their relationship with Solars; the Sun and Moon both stand far above the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've overwrought &quot;hero driven primarily by their emotions&quot; into &quot;barbarian king or queen.&quot; Conan and Khan Singh are clear examples of heroes driven to great deeds from desire. Kull is slightly more complex (as I type this I barely contain a laugh but it's true) in that he has desire and duty. Khal Drogo fits that at as well. I hesitate to speculate on whether Genghis Khan was a man driven by emotion since the remaining accounts of him are either from people he conquered or venerating him as a god-like figure, making it hard to truly judge what drove him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=67184#post67184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's room for a kind of &quot;hereditary&quot; shapeshifter, but it can't really be based on Lunars. I'd recommend something to do with animal gods or Gaia, but that would be redundant with Exigents or Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue you dismiss the possibility too soon. It's entirely possible to have hereditary shapeshifters based on Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. Literally based upon them; a specific ritual can bind a Lunar's animal spirit to a Dragon-Blooded's bloodline and &quot;corrupt&quot; it (in the eyes of the Immaculate Order, notionally) such that they can choose between humanoid form, animal form, and war form without the ability to acquire unrelated forms. How the binding is finally accomplished is, of course, best left to the discretion and proclivities of whatever group chooses to implement such an Exalt type.<br /> <br /> But we've digressed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T18:17:53-08:00","id":67545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/66728-why-are-the-lunars-celestial-exalted-as-we-understand-the-term?p=67184#post67184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about giving Creation itself its own Exalted champions?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got those - they're called &quot;the Exalted.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T18:23:22-08:00","id":67551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l-